SOAPBOX: "Competed" on 80m only ... the rest was opportunistic DXing ... nice opportunity! 80m score was 221 points * (13 + 43) = 12,376. QRP with single-wire antenna (1/4-wave vertical) can be discouraging at times, especially on 80m ... it takes a while for Europe to open to the point that I can be heard by even the best RX antennas ... many thanks for "good ears!". Worked a few new ones, though, adding 7 to my 80m list ... always fun to see them come through LOTW (I hope)! Rig: Hermes Lite 2 "rig-in-a-box" with Raspberry Pi 4 outdoors at base of 1/4-wave fan vertical (80m element is helically wound) with 32 radials, WiFi remote-controlled from office Windows laptop via Quisk Remote software transceiver running at both ends.
